There are several things to consider when designing a maintenance plan for remanufacturing. First, what is the scope of the remanufacturing process? What components need to be repaired or replaced? What is the expected lifetime of the remanufactured product?

Next, what is the frequency of maintenance? How often will the product need to be serviced? What is the expected wear and tear on the product?

Finally, what is the cost of maintenance? How much will it cost to repair or replace components? What is the expected cost of labour?